{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-fixed-point-set","title":"def:pet-ch5-fixed-point-set","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.md","line":860,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex#def:pet-ch5-fixed-point-set","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-exponential-map]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","label":"def:pet-ch5-fixed-point-set","line":1926,"source":"\\begin{definition}[fixed-point set; totally geodesic submanifold]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch5-fixed-point-set}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0215}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch5-exponential-map}\n\n  For a set $S$ of isometries of $(M,g)$, $\\operatorname{Fix}(S)=\\{x\\in M\\mid\n  F(x)=x\\ \\forall F\\in S\\}$. A submanifold $N\\subset(M,g)$ is \\emph{totally\n  geodesic} if for each $p\\in N$ a neighborhood of $0\\in T_pN\\subset T_pM$ is\n  mapped into $N$ by $\\exp_p$ (for $M$): geodesics of $N$ are geodesics of $M$, and\n  any $M$-geodesic tangent to $N$ at a point stays in $N$ for a short time.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[fixed-point set; totally geodesic submanifold] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368352d66697865642d706f696e742d736574\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0215</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23def%3Apet-ch5-exponential-map\">↗ def:pet-ch5-exponential-map</a> <p></p>For a set <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span> of isometries of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Fix}(S)=\\{ x\\in M\\mid F(x)=x\\  \\forall F\\in S\\} $\">$\\operatorname {Fix}(S)=\\{ x\\in M\\mid F(x)=x\\  \\forall F\\in S\\} $</span>. A submanifold <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N\\subset (M,g)$\">$N\\subset (M,g)$</span> is <em>totally geodesic</em> if for each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in N$\">$p\\in N$</span> a neighborhood of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0\\in T_pN\\subset T_pM$\">$0\\in T_pN\\subset T_pM$</span> is mapped into <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N$\">$N$</span> by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> (for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>): geodesics of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N$\">$N$</span> are geodesics of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>, and any <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>-geodesic tangent to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N$\">$N$</span> at a point stays in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N$\">$N$</span> for a short time. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-local-isometry-covering","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-fixed-tangent-subspace","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-exponential-map","title":"def:pet-ch5-exponential-map","label":"def:pet-ch5-exponential-map"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-fixed-tangent-subspac